      "sourceHash": "6f1ca80d48f3643f73c096ee4d50f5689cdea82f7fe83cc78d0773aecfb7c401",
      "originalSpan": "Your thyroid uses iodine to make thyroid hormones. However, if you have Hashimoto’s disease or other types of autoimmune thyroid disorders, you may be sensitive to iodine’s harmful side effects. Eating foods that have large amounts of iodine—such as kelp, dulse, or other kinds of seaweed—may cause or worsen hypothyroidism. Taking iodine supplements can have the same effect.",
